v {xschem version=3.4.7 file_version=1.2

* drclvs_testcell -- symbol for the DRC/LVS bring-up test cell (issue #14).
*
* Nothing instantiates this cell: it exists only so that xschem netlists
* drclvs_testcell.sch as a real `.subckt` with a fixed port order. Without a
* symbol xschem emits the commented `**.subckt` / `*.iopin` form, which is
* not what KLayout's SPICE reader (and therefore the gf180mcu LVS deck)
* consumes.
*
* PORT ORDER -- must match the ipin/opin/iopin order in the schematic, and
* is what layout/drclvs.py asserts against the layout's net labels:
*
*     D  G  S  VSS

}
G {}
K {type=subcircuit
format="@name @pinlist @symname"
template="name=x1"
}
V {}
S {}
E {}
P 4 5 -60 -40 60 -40 60 40 -60 40 -60 -40 {}
B 5 57.5 -32.5 62.5 -27.5 {name=D dir=inout}
L 7 60 -30 80 -30 {}
T {D} 55 -34 0 1 0.2 0.2 {}
B 5 -62.5 -12.5 -57.5 -7.5 {name=G dir=in}
L 7 -80 -10 -60 -10 {}
T {G} -55 -14 0 0 0.2 0.2 {}
B 5 57.5 7.5 62.5 12.5 {name=S dir=inout}
L 7 60 10 80 10 {}
T {S} 55 6 0 1 0.2 0.2 {}
B 5 -62.5 27.5 -57.5 32.5 {name=VSS dir=inout}
L 7 -80 30 -60 30 {}
T {VSS} -55 26 0 0 0.2 0.2 {}
T {@symname} -35 -6 0 0 0.3 0.3 {}
T {@name} -60 -52 0 0 0.2 0.2 {}
